      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding HEAD at the end breaks `writeConvertTable`\u0027s reflog loop. The refs get sorted by `sortAndWriteRefs`, but the logs are written in list order and \"HEAD\" sorts before \"refs/\". So any repo with an unborn HEAD where another ref has a reflog now fails with \"records must be increasing: last refs/heads/master, this HEAD\". Before this change, the same conversion just lost HEAD.\n\n```suggestion\n\t\t\trefs.add(0, head);\n```\n\nAlso, could the test also cover a branch that has a reflog? In `roundTripPreservesUnbornHeadAndReflog` the bare repo doesn\u0027t write one for `populated`.",
